      "title": "dfilter: Don't crash on vals for BASE_UNIT_STRING",
      "message": "dfilter: Don't crash on vals for BASE_UNIT_STRING\n\nMake sure we check for BASE_UNIT_STRING and don't treat it like\nan ordinary value string, with illegal memory accesses. For now,\nit's not supported (would it be that useful?)\n\nThis applies to both the vals() function and filters that attempt\nto match a numeric field with a string.\n\nBefore:\n\n$ ./run/dftest 'ipv6.hopopts.len_oct == \"test\"'\nFilter:\n ipv6.hopopts.len_oct == \"test\"\n\n=================================================================\n==3011913==ERROR: AddressSanitizer: global-buffer-overflow on address 0x7f4a7a177438 at pc 0x7f4a664738e9 bp 0x7fff9ca69b50 sp 0x7fff9ca69b48\nREAD of size 8 at 0x7f4a7a177438 thread T0\n    #0 0x7f4a664738e8 in mk_fvalue_from_hfinfo /home/johnthacker/wireshark/epan/dfilter/semcheck.c:556:16\n\nAfter:\n\n$ ./run/dftest 'ipv6.hopopts.len_oct == \"test\"'\nFilter:\n ipv6.hopopts.len_oct == \"test\"\n\nError: Unsigned integer (16 bits) cannot be converted from a string (\"test\").\n  ipv6.hopopts.len_oct == \"test\"\n                          ^~~~~~\n",
